  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1155 PM CST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nOn Wednesday the next weather system will likely eject out of the\ndesert southwest and move across the southern plains. This system\nhas a low chance to have moisture and thus will most likely be\ndry. So while this system wont produce rain it will produce windy\nconditions across the panhandles. These southerly winds will \ncontinue to draw up further warm air increasing the temperatures.\n\nA further weather system has increasing chances of ejecting out\ndesert southwest across the southern plains late Thursday through\nFriday. This system has a low to medium chance of being able to\nsource moisture and cause rain across the panhandles. This weather\nsystem just like all the previous one will most likely bring windy\nconditions with the southerly winds bringing up more warm air.\nThis will continue the warming trend across the panhandles through\nFriday. \n\nThen for the rest of the weekend the cold air associated with the\nweather system will likely push into the southern plains \nreversing the warming trend. This colder air is more likely than \nnot to be dry so fair and sunny weather is currently forecasted \nfor the weekend.",
